WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.790
This is really great.

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:06.359
Joe Biden is immediately handling the pandemic
and all of these different things.

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:09.940
Donald Trump is in court trying to get rid
of Obamacare.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.460
And yesterday, Joe Biden and Kamala Harris
held a press conference and they said we should

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.930
not be ending Obamacare at this point in time
now before we even get to any clips.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:26.009
It was sort of jarring to see Joe and Carmela
go a half hour without insulting anybody.

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:29.800
And when they took questions, Joe Biden actually
answered the questions.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.050
It was a nice change of pace.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:35.521
I've just become completely unaccustomed to
it over the last four years now when Joe Biden

00:00:35.521 --> 00:00:37.510
was asked questions.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.820
It's crazy that this is even noteworthy.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:46.040
He would listen to the question, pause to
think about an answer and then actually answer

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.130
the question.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.320
Mind blown, right.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.320
Incredible.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.580
And as you can imagine, most of the questions
Joe Biden was asked were about the fact that

00:00:54.580 --> 00:01:01.490
Trump continues to claim he won and that Biden
didn't win and Trump hasn't conceded and Joe

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.670
Biden played it really well.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:07.259
Here he is answering and laughing Trump off.

00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:09.840
And I'll tell you about the importance of
that in a moment.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.369
Presumably, at some point you will need access
to more classified information to secure facilities

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:15.659
and the like.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:17.560
What options are you considering?

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.960
How will you move ahead if the president continues
to refuse to concede?

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:31.719
Well, look, access to classified information
is is useful, but I'm not in a position to

00:01:31.719 --> 00:01:33.899
make any decisions on those issues anyway.

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:39.859
There's one, as I said, one president at a
time and he will be president until January

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:40.859
20th.

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:43.289
It would be nice to have it, but it's not
critical.

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:46.289
And that's we're just going to proceed the
way we have.

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:52.389
We're going to we're going to do exactly what
we'd be doing if he had conceded and said

00:01:52.389 --> 00:01:55.140
we have one, which we have.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.789
And so there's nothing really changing, but
not ruling out legal action.

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:01.719
So I don't see a need for legal action.

00:02:01.719 --> 00:02:03.119
Quite frankly.

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:09.270
I think the legal action is you're seeing
it play out, the actions he's taking.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:15.939
And so far, there is no evidence of any of
the assertions made by the president or Secretary

00:02:15.939 --> 00:02:22.370
of State Powell, Secretary of State Colin
Powell.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:29.800
So the calm is commendable and the laugh at
the end is just perfect as far as optics go.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:36.510
But what is really interesting to understand
is that as the narcissistic egomaniac that

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:42.989
is Donald Trump, narcissistic egomaniacs want
other people to be mad and they want other

00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:44.500
people to be afraid.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:50.470
We've talked to all sorts of different psychologists
and others on the program over the last four

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.650
years.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:57.580
And they have explained and this is widely
written about in literature, in psychology,

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:05.170
literature, that narcissists and these sort
of egomaniacs like Donald Trump, they control

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:11.230
situations by getting the other person angry,
by getting the other person rattled.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:17.060
And so Joe Biden just laughing it off and
moving full steam ahead with the transition

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.420
and a coronavirus task force and the some
of the same reporters who normally would be

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:25.599
sitting in the press briefing room asking
Trump questions are now at Joe Biden's press

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:26.930
conference.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.480
This has to be enraging Donald Trump.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.829
Now, Joe Biden was asked versions of that
same question, including does what Donald

00:03:34.829 --> 00:03:37.730
Trump is doing hurt your transition plan?

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.069
Does what Donald Trump is doing affect your
ability to do?

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:44.360
ABC and Joe Biden just very calmly saying
we're moving ahead.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:47.299
Donald Trump's behavior is not affecting my
transition.

00:03:47.299 --> 00:03:48.340
I'm the president elect.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.340
I'm moving forward.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.480
Thank you, Mr. President elect.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.390
During the campaign, you said you were not
naive about how difficult it would be to unite

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:58.140
the country.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.120
It's now three days after you were projected
as the president elect.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.379
The president himself says he has won this
election.

00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:09.500
His own administration has not moved forward
to give you access to what you need to do

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.110
to begin the work of your transition.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:15.700
Just a few minutes ago, the secretary of state
when asked if he would.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:20.319
Cooperate with a smooth transition, he said
there will be a smooth transition to a second

00:04:20.319 --> 00:04:21.319
Trump administration.

00:04:21.319 --> 00:04:26.819
I wonder if you have a message for the president
who may well be watching right now, and how

00:04:26.819 --> 00:04:30.880
do you expect to be able to work with Republicans
when so many have thus far refused to even

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.100
acknowledge your victory?

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:37.590
Well, first of all, we are at the beginning
of the transition.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.889
We're well underway.

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:47.690
And the ability for the administration in
any way by failing to recognize this is our

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:53.210
win does not change the dynamic at all and
what we're able to do.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:56.970
And then Joe Biden interestingly, pointed
out that he thinks Republicans are standing

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.730
by Trump because they're scared or intimidated
by him.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:10.280
And there's a lot of interesting stuff to
discuss there as well.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:15.250
Mr. President elect Senate Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell has suggested today that he

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:22.200
may not recognize the outcome of this election
until the Electoral College meets next month.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:28.270
Have you spoken to your long time friend in
the Senate, Mr. McConnell?

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:33.190
And what do you make of his specific comments
over the last 24 hours?

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:36.680
I haven't had a chance to speak to Mitch.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:42.430
My expectation is that I will do that not
too distant future.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:49.340
I think that the whole Republican Party has
been put in a position with a few notable

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:59.449
exceptions, of being mildly intimidated by
the sitting president.

00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:03.389
Yeah, what's interesting about that and our
friend Bill Share and others have been tweeting

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:10.490
about this, it is very interesting that even
as a loser, Republicans still seem to be under

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.970
the thumb of Donald Trump.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.570
Now, this could be for a few different reasons.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:17.789
There could be Republicans who still think
maybe Trump gets another four years.

00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:20.479
And so I should sort of stay on his good side.

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:25.919
It could be that it's merely concern over
the Georgia Senate races.

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:28.660
And once those are done, they will bail on
Trump.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:32.419
Now, of course, at that point, it will only
be 15 days until Trump leaves office.

00:06:32.419 --> 00:06:34.210
I don't know.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:40.870
We streamed this event live and many of our
viewers reacted to Biden's calm by saying

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:43.599
Biden being calm is making me calm.

00:06:43.599 --> 00:06:47.330
When Trump is manic and going crazy, my blood
pressure goes up.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:49.139
This is a lot of our viewers.

00:06:49.139 --> 00:06:52.930
Biden being so calm is making me calm, which
is interesting.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:59.240
And then lastly, here's Joe Biden making the
point that Trump not conceding makes Trump

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:02.900
look bad in bringing up the idea of Trump's
legacy.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:09.099
Sir, what do you say to the Americans that
are anxious over the fact that President Trump

00:07:09.099 --> 00:07:12.380
has yet to concede and what that might mean
for the country?

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:19.009
Well, I just think it's an embarrassment,
quite frankly.

00:07:19.009 --> 00:07:25.020
The only thing that how can I say this tactfully?

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:33.229
I think it will not help the president's legacy.

00:07:33.229 --> 00:07:41.220
I think that I know from my discussions with
foreign leaders thus far that they are hopeful

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:47.030
that the United States democratic institutions
are viewed once again as being strong and

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.030
enduring.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:52.550
Given how Donald Trump has been behaving,
it would actually be completely appropriate

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:58.020
for Joe Biden to attack Donald Trump, and
it would be totally appropriate for Joe Biden

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.710
to go after Donald Trump in a more serious
way.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.030
And yet he didn't.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:06.330
We are not going to agree with Joe Biden on
policy, on nearly everything.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:08.689
But there is a change in the air.

00:08:08.689 --> 00:08:12.400
Since Joe Biden was declared president elect
by networks, it's been palpable.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:17.889
And even many who did not vote for Biden in
the primary, but ultimately did vote for Joe

00:08:17.889 --> 00:08:22.539
Biden in in the general election with some
skepticism, have emailed me and said, you

00:08:22.539 --> 00:08:25.310
know, it's not about policy right now.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:32.779
I'm finding Joe's demeanor in the face of
unhinged insanity from Trump and endless conspiracy

00:08:32.779 --> 00:08:33.979
theories from the right.

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:38.469
I'm finding Joe Biden's demeanor to be the
right fit for the time.

00:08:38.469 --> 00:08:39.990
Let's hope it continues.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:45.730
And we have so much more to talk about today
about the conspiracy theories and the allegations

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:51.850
and so much more, including Secretary of State
Mike Pompeo asked about the fact that there's

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:56.890
been no acknowledgment of Joe Biden's when
Mike Pompeo saying there will be a smooth

00:08:56.890 --> 00:09:00.829
transition to a second Trump administration.

00:09:00.829 --> 00:09:02.220
That's coming up a little bit later.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:10:19.190
Make sure you're following me on Twitter,
where you can find me at department T

